we model three different type of  Landscapes that are typically used in  arid regions and that includes music  Zurich and Oasis landscape I think a  better way to understand them is to  think of them as three different type of  cars  magic  landscape is like High Juice water  landscape so I I like to call it like a  gas guzzling car that is classic car  that is aesthetically pleasant but in  the long run it's not really efficient  um the other type of landscape or the  other end of the spectrum is Zurich  landscape which are very precise water  use or low water use and I like to call  it electrical car because it's not  really consuming a lot of gas  and then in the middle is the Oasis  landscape with a medium water use and  it's precisely the cocktail of two these  two to Landscapes which in this case I  like to say hybrid car but that Oasis  landscape is what we found in our study  to be much more efficient in overall and  that efficiency is in terms of outdoor  thermal Comforts and irrigation water  requirement and what we found was that  um  Oasis landscape's temperature was  comparable to the magic landscape which  is supposed to be cooler at the noon  time  and then what surprised us was that it's  at the night time the it's temperature  profile was comparable to the xeric  landscape which is the low water use  landscape and even those Eric landscape  had  four degrees cooling at the nighttime  magic had eight degrees cooling at that  point and so that kind of was surprising  to us as to how the ulyssa's landscape  had this dual personality and I think  when it comes to irrigation water  requirement the results were pretty  counter not counter intuitive where  music has higher water use overall and  then Oasis had  you know was the second higher  um water user so  yeah those were our findings
 

